  "details": "Update: This issue was likely related to Postprocessing issues that were present on the oculus VRC client; with the resolution of that issue, this issue was also resolved.\n\nHello,\nAfter the most recent updates, I've found that having any 3.0 avatar in view absolutely annihilates my framerate, making it quite hard to stay in that \"world\" for prolonged periods of time as it induces sickness and frequent crashes.\nI do not know if this is an issue specific to my hardware but the impact is very clear.\nHiding/showing the 3.0 avatar in question has a VERY notable impact and is easy to spot.\nGraphics: RTX 30 series\nCPU: Ryzen 9 3900x \nHMD: Oculus (Rift S)\nIf anyone else here has tested this, please leave your input on this.\nThanks!\n-Fuzzout\n\n\nThe below error is the final entry in the VRChat log as my game unceremoneously froze and shut down; the behavior of the client was precisely what I've observed before when quickly turning my head and having 3.0 avatar go in/out of view.\n\nError      -  A multisampled texture being bound to a non-multisampled sampler. Disabling in order to avoid undefined behavior. Please use Texture2DMS in the shader.",
